            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Mistake 3: Selling during a downturn. Market declines are normal and expected. The S&P 500 has experienced an average intra-year decline of approximately 14% every single year, yet it has delivered positive annual returns in roughly 75% of calendar years. Selling during a decline locks in your losses permanently. Staying invested allows you to participate in the recovery."
